<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.3.xsd">

    <!--
    Structure of segmented logs: nesting, retry attempts, loop iterations, error handlers and threads.

    PROCESS_LOG_SEGMENTS is large (and partitioned by day on big installations):
    - all columns are nullable without defaults, so adding them doesn't rewrite the table;
    - a single ALTER, so the exclusive lock on the table (and every partition) is taken once;
    - lock_timeout: fail (and retry on the next start) instead of blocking the segment inserts
      while waiting for long-running queries;
    - can be applied manually beforehand, the changeset is skipped if the columns exist.
    -->
    <changeSet id="2461001" author="ybrigo@gmail.com">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="PROCESS_LOG_SEGMENTS" columnName="SEGMENT_THREAD"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>

        <sql>
            set local lock_timeout = '5s';

            alter table PROCESS_LOG_SEGMENTS
                add column if not exists PARENT_SEGMENT_ID bigint,
                add column if not exists SEGMENT_ATTEMPT smallint,
                add column if not exists SEGMENT_LOOP_INDEX int,
                add column if not exists SEGMENT_ROLE smallint,
                add column if not exists SEGMENT_THREAD int;
        </sql>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
    Deployment requirement for partitioned PROCESS_EVENTS installations:

    The automatic changeset below is intentionally marked ran when PROCESS_EVENTS is a
    declarative partitioned table or an inheritance parent. Operators must build the matching
    index on every storage-bearing relation. Run every generated CREATE INDEX statement outside
    a transaction:

    WITH RECURSIVE event_relations AS (
        SELECT c.oid, n.nspname, c.relname, c.relkind, 0 AS depth
        FROM pg_catalog.pg_class c
        JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
        WHERE n.nspname = current_schema() AND c.relname = 'process_events'
        UNION ALL
        SELECT child.oid, child_ns.nspname, child.relname, child.relkind, parent.depth + 1
        FROM event_relations parent
        JOIN pg_catalog.pg_inherits i ON i.inhparent = parent.oid
        JOIN pg_catalog.pg_class child ON child.oid = i.inhrelid
        JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace child_ns ON child_ns.oid = child.relnamespace
    )
    SELECT format(
        'CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY %I ON %I.%I (INSTANCE_ID, INSTANCE_CREATED_AT, ((EVENT_DATA::jsonb ->> %L)::varchar), EVENT_SEQ) WHERE EVENT_TYPE = %L;',
        'ix_' || substr(md5(nspname || '.' || relname || '.logSegmentId'), 1, 24),
        nspname, relname, 'logSegmentId', 'ELEMENT')
    FROM event_relations
    WHERE relkind = 'r'
    ORDER BY depth DESC, nspname, relname;

    For declarative partitioning, create the same index on every partitioned parent with
    CREATE INDEX <collision-safe-name> ON ONLY <schema>.<parent> (...), using the expression and
    predicate above. Then attach each child index with ALTER INDEX
    <schema>.<parent-index> ATTACH PARTITION <schema>.<child-index>, working bottom-up from the
    deepest parent before attaching its index to the root. Derive every per-table name as
    ix_ plus the first 24 characters of md5(schema || '.' || table || '.logSegmentId'), matching
    the generator, so names are stable and collision-safe.

    For inheritance partitioning, the storage query includes both every child and the queried
    parent because all have relkind 'r'; all of them must be indexed. The site's child-creation
    procedure or template must also create this exact expression/predicate index, with the same
    collision-safe naming rule, on every future inheritance child before that child accepts
    PROCESS_EVENTS rows. PostgreSQL does not inherit the parent's index. This is an ongoing
    provisioning requirement, not only a one-time deployment operation.
    -->
    <changeSet id="2461010" author="ybrigo@gmail.com" runInTransaction="false">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <indexExists
                        tableName="PROCESS_EVENTS"
                        indexName="IDX_PROC_EVENTS_LOG_SEGMENT"/>
            </not>
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT count(*)
                FROM pg_catalog.pg_class c
                JOIN pg_catalog.pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
                WHERE n.nspname = current_schema()
                  AND c.relname = 'process_events'
                  AND c.relkind = 'r'
                  AND NOT EXISTS (
                      SELECT 1
                      FROM pg_catalog.pg_inherits i
                      WHERE i.inhparent = c.oid
                  )
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>

        <sql>
            CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IDX_PROC_EVENTS_LOG_SEGMENT
                ON PROCESS_EVENTS (
                    INSTANCE_ID,
                    INSTANCE_CREATED_AT,
                    ((EVENT_DATA::jsonb ->> 'logSegmentId')::varchar),
                    EVENT_SEQ
                )
                WHERE EVENT_TYPE = 'ELEMENT'
        </sql>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
